  "status": "Real V8 end-block uninitialized reads root-caused and fixed in native graph controls. Patch18 and native RPM regression prepared; complete updated RPM and native ARM qualification remain required.",
  "root_cause": "RawMachineAssembler::MakeReschedulable declares current_control and current_effect for each block. The end-block branch merges terminal controls but assigns neither local, then falls through to copying both indeterminate pointers into final-state tables. The end block has no nodes, terminator or successors requiring that state.",
  "fix": "Finish the end-block iteration immediately after merging terminal controls, with debug assertions for the structural invariants. Other blocks and loop-backedge repair retain their existing behavior. No default pointer, disabled warning or bypassed check is introduced.",
  "source_invariants": "Schedule constructs end as an empty block with kNone control and no control input. RawMachineAssembler never binds it as a current code block; terminal instructions add incoming edges. EnsureCFGWellFormedness excludes end from critical-edge splitting. No successor consumes final-state entries for end.",
  "native_tests": {
    "cases_per_execution": 700,
    "shapes": [
      "single return",
      "two branch returns",
      "merge with Phi and return",
      "infinite loop",
      "normal return and deferred throw",
      "three-way switch",
      "loop with backedge and exit return"
    ],
    "assertions": "Actual V8 TFGraph, Zone, Schedule and RawMachineAssembler are used. Every graph has the expected terminal input count and exact Return/Throw/Terminate opcode counts; the accounting allocator returns to zero.",
    "ordinary_baseline": "700 cases pass normally and under Memcheck; copying the unused indeterminate pointers alone does not trigger ordinary Memcheck.",
    "instrumented_baseline": "700 cases preserve graph outputs but report 1200 undefined-value client checks from exactly two contexts. Diagnostic-only MAKE_MEM_UNDEFINED marks each fresh local lifetime; CHECK_MEM_IS_DEFINED inspects both pointers immediately before their original stores.",
    "fixed": "700 cases pass both normally and under Memcheck for the uninstrumented and instrumented fixes. Both runs report zero errors and free all 3602 allocations.",
    "compiler": "The original standalone source reproduces the two maybe-uninitialized warnings. Both fixed source variants compile without diagnostics.",
    "package_helper": "Five unit tests cover native ABI/hardening/warning preservation, LTO modes, quoted paths and literal shell characters, receipt content handling, and eleven malformed command forms. The combined dependency/helper test run passes."
  },
  "link_configuration": "Controls link actual freshly built V8 native compiler/base archives, with matching package feature and ABI defines. They build graphs only and do not create an Isolate or execute generated code. V8's unmodified snapshot-empty, embedded-empty and setup-isolate-deserialize sources satisfy unused startup references. This is a diagnostic link configuration only; the packaged regression requires the complete actual generated snapshot archive.",
  "qualification_limits": [
    "Only diagnostic variants contain Memcheck requests. They do not change control flow or pointer values. Production patch has only the end-block assertions and continue.",
    "Native archive sections are used without LTO for these standalone memory controls. The runtime package retains its normal LTO configuration and still must pass the complete RPM build.",
    "Initial full-archive linking failed while archive compilation was incomplete; later links lacked startup snapshot definitions. Those failures are preserved and not counted as passing qualification.",
    "The initial instrumented compile lacked Memcheck development headers. The successful run mounts the host client-request headers; runtime memory checking uses the pinned Leap Valgrind image.",
    "Full generated-snapshot helper execution and native ARM remain open gates. No package upload or publication is implied by these focused results."
  ],
